        "href": "#C4"
      },
      {
        "text": "C5\nThe mocked CLI entry test is deleted; built package entries gain execution and platform-specific cleanup tests.",
        "href": "#C5"
      },
      {
        "text": "C6\nThe temporary policy-testing export, its import restriction and two lint tests are retired together.",
        "href": "#C6"
      },
      {
        "text": "C7\nPackage test files run serially; the fixture environment adds tsx and local test helpers.",
        "href": "#C7"
      },
      {
        "text": "C8\nCLI worker timing and mismatch-initialization assertions are removed; direct executor version rejection is restored.",
        "href": "#C8"
      },
      {
        "text": "Give hosts a client\n↗",
        "href": "#unit-4"
      },
      {
        "text": "D1\nA Node-free public facade loads a Node runtime at construction; only execute/control cross the new host boundary.",
        "href": "#D1"
      },
      {
        "text": "D2\nOrdered lazy guards stop later observations: disabled → record → starting → version → responsiveness.",
        "href": "#D2"
      },
      {
        "text": "D3\nAbsent/dead/incompatible routes trigger independent startup; local attempts get a fresh executor and keep their chosen mode.",
        "href": "#D3"
      },
      {
        "text": "D4\nWarm failures retry locally only when transport marks them safe; uncertain/accepted failures return controlled output.",
        "href": "#D4"
      },
      {
        "text": "D5\nThe client owns warm output capture in the OS temp directory, failure bytes and malformed-output cleanup.",
        "href": "#D5"
      },
      {
        "text": "D6\nControl has typed start/status/stop results, a separate status timeout, disabled-start short circuit and propagated errors.",
        "href": "#D6"
      },
      {
        "text": "D7\nThe host supplies readiness command/argv through startup, preserving the queued executor probe.",
        "href": "#D7"
      },
